  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "1. Weights and activations sit in GDDR6, 48 GB with ECC — identical capacity to L40.",
      "focus": ["gddr-left", "gddr-right"],
      "dot": "gddr-left",
      "explode": 0.6,
      "drill": null,
      "stage": "gddr"
    },
    {
      "text": "2. The 384-bit memory controller reads GDDR6 at up to 864 GB/s, same as L40 — this part of the pipeline is unchanged.",
      "focus": ["mc"],
      "dot": "mc",
      "stage": "memory-controller"
    },
    {
      "text": "3. Data lands in the 96 MB L2 cache, buffering hot weights and KV cache for AI inference and training batches.",
      "focus": ["l2"],
      "dot": "l2",
      "stage": "l2"
    },
    {
      "text": "4. Tiles move into each SM's 128 KB L1/shared memory.",
      "focus": ["sm-a"],
      "dot": "sm-a",
      "drill": "sm-detail",
      "stage": "shared-memory"
    },
    {
      "text": "5. One of 568 fourth-gen Tensor Cores runs the Transformer Engine's FP8 matmul. Same silicon as L40, but L40S's higher sustained clocks under its 350W budget push the rated throughput to 733 TFLOPS dense FP8 (1,466 with sparsity) — roughly 2x L40's listed figures.",
      "focus": ["tensor-core"],
      "dot": "tensor-core",
      "drill": "sm-detail",
      "stage": "tensor-core"
    },
    {
      "text": "6. In parallel, one of 142 third-gen RT Cores remains available for ray-traced rendering, though AI training/inference is the primary workload this card targets.",
      "focus": ["rt-core"],
      "dot": "rt-core",
      "drill": "sm-detail",
      "stage": "rt-core"
    },
    {
      "text": "7. Partial sums accumulate in the register file.",
      "focus": ["register-file"],
      "dot": "register-file",
      "drill": "sm-detail",
      "stage": "accumulate"
    },
    {
      "text": "8. Epilogue: the warp scheduler and CUDA cores apply bias, activation, or quantize the result back down.",
      "focus": ["warp-scheduler"],
      "dot": "warp-scheduler",
      "drill": "sm-detail",
      "stage": "epilogue"
    },
    {
      "text": "9. Results write back through L2 to GDDR6. The display engine's DisplayPort outputs exist on-die but ship disabled by default — L40S is meant to run headless in an AI server rack.",
      "focus": ["l2", "display-engine"],
      "dot": "l2",
      "drill": null,
      "stage": "writeback"
    },
    {
      "text": "10. With no NVLink, multi-GPU traffic and host transfers go out over PCIe Gen4 x16, same as L40.",
      "focus": ["pcie"],
      "dot": "pcie",
      "drill": null,
      "stage": "pcie"
    }
  ],
